## Final Direction

**Build CilikLab as a coherent, attractive, student-friendly coding education platform—not an overloaded enterprise dashboard.**

Prioritize the learning journey:

**Discover a class → Enroll → Learn a concept → Write code → Run and inspect the result → Receive progressive hints → Improve the solution → Reflect on changes → Get teacher feedback → Track progress.**

Make the teacher experience equally coherent:

**Create a class → Prepare exercises → Monitor progress → Review attempts → Identify support needs → Help students → Reuse guidance → Evaluate class outcomes.**

Every major feature should support one of these two journeys.

Use good design judgment. Prefer a small number of well-designed, useful components over a large number of crowded cards. Make the interface feel consistent, approachable, modern, and ready to demonstrate to educators, students, and competition evaluators.

